<title>SPAIN: Cantabrico to stick to electric protocol.</title>
<headline>Cantabrico to stick to electric protocol.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish utility Hidroelectrica del Cantabrico has now decided to adhere to Spain's electricity protocol, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>In December, Cantabrico was the only utility which had refused to sign agreement because it was not satisfied with provisions allocated to it to recover stranded costs.</p>
<p>The sector-wide accord mapped out a framework to open it up to competition by the turn of the century.</p>
<p>The firm will make a statement later today on the change in its stance, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>--Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
